The Skills (and other prompts-based) list in the Agent Customizations editor was clipped at the bottom — the last item(s) were always partially or fully hidden regardless of scroll position.

**Root cause:** `AICustomizationListWidget.layout()` set an explicit pixel height on its element, causing it to overflow `prompts-content-container` (which has `padding: 40px 40px 16px` and `overflow: hidden`). The bottom ~56px of the list were permanently clipped.

**Fix:** Mirror the approach already used by `McpListWidget.layout()`:
- Clear the explicit height style so CSS `height: 100%` resolves within the padded container
- Read `clientHeight` for the actual available space, falling back to the passed `height` when the element is hidden

```typescript
// Before
this.element.style.height = `${height}px`;
// ...
const listHeight = Math.max(0, height - searchBarHeight - headerHeight);

// After
this.element.style.height = '';
// ...
const availableHeight = this.element.clientHeight || height;
const listHeight = Math.max(0, availableHeight - searchBarHeight - headerHeight);
```

